concepts.content:
When working with two-dimensional (2D) images, partial derivatives can be approximated along the $n$ and $m$ components using kernels such as:
$$
\begin{bmatrix}
  1 \\
  -1
\end{bmatrix}
~~~~~~~
\begin{bmatrix}
  1 & -1
\end{bmatrix}
$$
A limitation of this discretization is that filters of length 2 shift the output image by half a pixel, leading to spatial misalignment. This can be addressed by using alternative operators like the Roberts cross, which uses a rotated reference frame.

