concepts.content:
The Roberts cross operator is a 2D derivative discretization that removes spatial misalignment by using a rotated reference frame. It was introduced in 1963 and is defined by the following kernels:
$$
\begin{bmatrix}
  1 & ~0\\
  0 & -1
\end{bmatrix}
~~~~~~~
\begin{bmatrix}
  ~0 & 1 \\
  -1 & 0
\end{bmatrix}
$$

